cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Fence: Flagging the Parts of a Coding-Agent Pull Request That Go Beyond Its Issue"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jain
    given-names: Harshul
repository-code: "https://github.com/ReviewDebtZero/rd0-fence"
url: "https://rd0-fence.netlify.app"
abstract: >-
  Fence compares a pull request with the issue it closes and flags each changed part that goes beyond
  what the issue asked for, with a reason. It is pure Python, runs on CPU and needs no API key.
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - code review
  - scope creep
  - pull requests
  - GitHub Action
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
